# Harness run artifacts (regenerated on every run — do not commit)
*.log
*.stdout
*.out
recon_*.txt
# ⛔ ANCHORED ON PURPOSE — the leading `/` means "this directory only", never `evidence/`.
# The convention drifted from `foo.stdout` to `foo.stdout.txt` and this rule did not follow, so
# 40 loose driver captures sat untracked for weeks. That is not clutter: it made the tree
# permanently dirty, so the SessionStart hook reported "uncommitted changes — pull SKIPPED" at
# EVERY session start, training the next agent to wave past the one warning that protects a
# project worked on from several machines.
# ‼ A bare `*.stdout.txt` here would ALSO swallow `evidence/*.stdout.txt` — 92 files that are
# tracked DELIBERATELY as the project's evidence record — and every future one, silently.
# Fault-tested both ways on 2026-09-03: `git check-ignore` fires on a loose capture and does
# NOT fire on an evidence file.
/*.stdout.txt
# New states drivers write land in saves/ — commit only curated checkpoints, not scratch
saves/2*.ss1
saves/midstuck.ss1
livetest-runs/
x4-runs/
.gate-logs/
